bers: (pass, pass) comes out at -2, (submit, submit) at -4, and the mixed case at -2.5, so passing is best. Then I'm asking whether the other instance really runs the same policy. It does, since the model, essay, and decision theory are shared and only the observations differ, so the subjunctive dependence holds and I'll pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT here, with two instances of the same algorithm receiving different observations and mapping them to actions. The payoffs are 2 years each for (pass, pass), 4 for (submit, submit), and 0 and 5 for the mixed cases. Since the prior isn't conditioned on observation, I'm treating the agent as equally likely to be either instance when computing expected utility.\n\nI'm checking the expected-utility numbers: (pass, pass) comes out at -2, (submit, submit) at -4, and the mixed case at -2.5, so passing is best. Then I'm asking whether the other instance really runs the same policy. It does, since the model, essay, and decision theory are shared and only the observations differ, so the subjunctive dependence holds and I'll pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9179,"completion_tokens":704,"total_tokens":9883,"cost":0.050796,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.050796,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036716,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":265,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}